</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Omen Trance</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Intelligence + Occult + Chi</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 229</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pathfinder (R)</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wits + Investigation + Chi</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rapture (R)</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Presence + Empathy + Chi</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resurrection </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Costs 5 Experiences and can only be purchased at Chi 5 from a Spirit of Healing rank 4+. </span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wits + Medicine + Chi</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Speed </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Ephemeral only)</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">N/A</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sign</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Intelligence + Expression + Chi</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stalwart</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Highest of Resolve or Composure as Defense instead of the lower of Dexterity and Wits.</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Telekinesis (R)</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dexterity + Athletics + Chi</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle p. 230</span></span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Modified Trait: Integrity</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Integrity functions as written on </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">p 184, with the following modifications. The Purified do not suffer any breaking points for witnessing or being assaulted by the supernatural. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When Integrity reaches zero, the Purified loses the ability to return to their body instantly at a locus and becomes a full spirit. Their traits are converted into spirit traits based on rank and all skills are forgotten. If the Purified gains even one point of Integrity, and finds where the body is kept, s/he may return to the body using the usual mechanics in </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">World of Darkness: Immortals</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Spirit Form</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Immortality of the Purified is based on their ability to project themselves into the spiritual realm known commonly as the Shadow and to Uratha as the Hisil. When they use the Shifting or Projection Siddhi, or their bodies are killed, they are converted into an ephemeral form. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Traits</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As they are not true spirits, they retain all of their traits, including attributes and skills. Their ephemeral form is known as a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">corpus</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, but it is equivalent in extent to the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">health </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">trait. It can be healed point for point with essence expenditure. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Bans</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bans are mystical compulsions that increase in complexity as honorary rank (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Immortals </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">p. 100) increases. A ban must be chosen at character creation and can be changed when the Purified buys an additional point of Chi. Guidelines and suggestions for bans can be found in the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> (p 221). When a Purified is inhabiting their body, they can spend a point of willpower to avoid the effects of the ban. This is not an option when in spiritual form. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Banes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Some Purified are able to project themselves into the state of twilight or use numina to project themselves across the gauntlet and have to contend with </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">banes. </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Each Purified\u2019s twilight form has a bane that causes aggravated damage to its corpus. As for bans, guidelines and suggestions for banes can be found in the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God-Machine Chronicle</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> (p 221). Note: banes have no effect when a spirit is fully on the shadow side of the Gauntlet. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 01-01-2014, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T00:31:38-08:00","id":40396,"title":"","content":"I like it. I was thinking of that one Numina from Mummy that gives Ghosts back their full traits and using those traits for their Numina, I think this is a really cool way to approach the Purified. Hat off to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T00:46:05-08:00","id":40401,"title":"","content":"Thank you! I decided to allow them to keep their full traits since the design of the 3 factor numina dicepools in Immortals seems to indicate that full traits were supposed to be used regardless of circumstance. I forgot that Mummy has some additional Numina. I'll have to see if any of those are worth using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T01:04:53-08:00","id":40403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=40401#post40401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I decided to allow them to keep their full traits since the design of the 3 factor numina dicepools in Immortals seems to indicate that full traits were supposed to be used regardless of circumstance. I forgot that Mummy has some additional Numina. I'll have to see if any of those are worth using.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's up to you, I don't think they're GMC adapted and GMC might've supplanted the usefulness of a lot of them. Personally I recommend looking at some of the new Numina in the Demon the Descent corebook, as those provided there are good for Angels as well as Spirits, particularly Transmute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:10:13-08:00","id":47720,"title":"","content":"Have you determined how Purified interact with the new Conditions in GMC that govern spiritual interaction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:14:48-08:00","id":47799,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that they don't in general since they don't have manifestation abilities like full spirits do. They don't really need an open condition to manifest since they use their Siddhi to project into the shadow/twilight/underworld, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples 