ivider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:09:10-07:00","id":162751,"title":"","content":"I literally just joined the forums so I could respond to this. I love Immortals and have been thinking about this for a while now. Having played a Purified PC in a game for a few years, I can definitely say that I love it. On the other hand, I think that Purified lack a lot of the problems of other creatures in the World of Darkness in that they don't have to struggle constantly against a Beast like Kindred or deal with the aftermath of being Abducted like Changelings, the Fallen World effects in Mage, &amp;c. They are, to put it bluntly, actually awesome.<br /> <br /> My thoughts about Purified and GMC are ways in which I would improve Purified to be less amazingly awesome so that they can suffer from the same problems as every other end-point supernatural. I have decided that the real horror for Purified is that they are probably 100% spirit and just in denial about it.<br /> <br /> To that end, I wrote up all of my brainstorming and put it in a Google Doc, linked below. A lot of it is based on things I've read on this thread, but I've added a lot of things based on constantly ruminating on the ideas I expressed above. My GM experience is limited to Changeling and Mage, so I'd be happy to hear what people with broader GM experience think about all of this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Also, the URL below isn't working, nor is it letting me change it to something with an actual path, so here: <a href=\"http://bit.ly/1nthGj1\" target=\"_blank\">http://bit.ly/1nthGj1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","user":"quantumelody","date":".  The first URL did not work. :) 06-08-2014, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:48:47-07:00","id":162843,"title":"","content":"This is my favorite thing, quantumelody. Purified are a brilliant but under-developed concept. Thank you x100.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 06-08-2014, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:41:58-07:00","id":163070,"title":"","content":"Also, I have enabled commenting as of twenty minutes ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T20:17:08-07:00","id":163083,"title":"","content":"Question about your conception of the Purified: Are they human souls warped into Spirits, or Spirits that are created in the image of a human soul, consumed in the process? I think some of the assumptions being made about them forgetting human language and the like might be a bit unfounded if they're the former, but the latter would make sense.<br /> <br /> Of course, that could arguably be one of the questions the Purified ask themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T04:30:44-07:00","id":163388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=163083#post163083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about your conception of the Purified: Are they human souls warped into Spirits, or Spirits that are created in the image of a human soul, consumed in the process? I think some of the assumptions being made about them forgetting human language and the like might be a bit unfounded if they're the former, but the latter would make sense.<br /> <br /> Of course, that could arguably be one of the questions the Purified ask themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming the latter is actually the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:28:47-07:00","id":163448,"title":"","content":"Ooh, that's lovely.Reading it through.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aww, no overhaul of the Siddhi? Half of them are part of the basic rules for interacting with Ephemeral beings now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-09-2014, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T08:13:04-07:00","id":163599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quantumelody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=162751#post162751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally just joined the forums so I could respond to this. I love Immortals and have been thinking about this for a while now. Having played a Purified PC in a game for a few years, I can definitely say that I love it. On the other hand, I think that Purified lack a lot of the problems of other creatures in the World of Darkness in that they don't have to struggle constantly against a Beast like Kindred or deal with the aftermath of being Abducted like Changelings, the Fallen World effects in Mage, &amp;c. They are, to put it bluntly, actually awesome.<br /> <br /> My thoughts about Purified and GMC are ways in which I would improve Purified to be less amazingly awesome so that they can suffer from the same problems as every other end-point supernatural. I have decided that the real horror for Purified is that they are probably 100% spirit and just in denial about it.<br /> <br /> To that end, I wrote up all of my brainstorming and put it in a Google Doc, linked below. A lot of it is based on things I've read on this thread, but I've added a lot of things based on constantly ruminating on the ideas I expressed above. My GM experience is limited to Changeling and Mage, so I'd be happy to hear what people with broader GM experience think about all of this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, the URL below isn't working, nor is it letting me change it to something with an actual path, so here: <a href=\"http://bit.ly/1nthGj1\" target=\"_blank\">http://bit.ly/1nthGj1</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is most impressive, Quantumelody!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:34:46-07:00","id":163834,"title":"","content":"I am currently storytelling werewolf, and have a player character which just became Purified. (That was a fun story to run on its own; she was a <i>Second Sight</i> shaman, and the cord that tethered her to her body was cut, so she discorporated; it's been a long, trying hike back from the spirit wilds, changing and being bound into webs of obligation as she goes. If there's a chance for it, I highly recommend role-playing out the experience.) Anyway, I did a full, personal write-up for the splat, which drew heavily on your work here, Octavo.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly speaking up because I also gave Purified access to influences, however I handled them rather differently. Since spirits <i>are </i>their influences, I gave them influences which relate to aspects of their psyche: virtue, vice, beliefs, personality traits, existing derangements, concept, narrative or social role, Jungian archetypes - essentially, Astral influences which would apply to them as a character. Picking up new influences from spirits would be hard (without becoming magath), but they are able to pick them up from ghosts and astral figments (or perhaps angels). I also decided that at Chi 7 (spirit rank 5), they can gain the influence &quot;Humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> My Purified character also has a warped ephemeral form - exaggerated by her influence dots - and a spirit name, both of which make her easy to mistake as an abstract spirit, for those who aren't already familiar with the rare choir of human spirits.<br /> <br /> I agree with quantumelody in how handle the &quot;downside&quot; to being Purified - that they are actually spirits now - but I didn't expand on that very much. In <i>Immortals</i>, it's explained that they get woven into the politics of the Shadow, in service to choirs and incarnae as a world-walking agent; that, along with the ordinary limitations that come with spirits, is all I have planned. But I do like the emphasis on new sensations, and growing disconnect to humanity as their new morality trait (on the other hand, that may be counterproductive with my assumptions that they are humanity spirits; then again, it could be a disconnect from their human life and a pull toward humanity in general . . . )<br /> <br /> I have the feeling the way I've written up Purified for my game is going to quickly lead to a over-powered character, to the point of only working well in mage chronicles. However, my game is nearly at 700 exp (pre-gmc system) so everything is kind of skewed in that direction . . . <br /> <br /> I rather like the Purified as a template, and expanding the rules for them is something I'm particularly interested in. I've enjoyed reading everyone else's approach to the subject quite a bit. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xc4XmROQ-hDKhsQdhrQWK5KpK-8OhlkFnrPcyTaUlgc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's my write-up</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:18:14-07:00","id":163883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=163834#post163834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently storytelling werewolf, and have a player character which just became Purified. (That was a fun story to run on its own; she was a <i>Second Sight</i> shaman, and the cord that tethered her to her body was cut, so she discorporated; it's been a long, trying hike back from the spirit wilds, changing and being bound into webs of obligation as she goes. If there's a chance for it, I highly recommend role-playing out the experience.) Anyway, I did a full, personal write-up for the splat, which drew heavily on your work here, Octavo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very glad to hear my writeup was helpful! <br /> <br /> I think I may need to incorporate the way you added influences. There's also some other precedent for that - Ghost Mages and the Scions of God from MtAw both had their arcana represented as influences. Definitely digging how the Purified's influences draw on &quot;virtue, vice, beliefs, personality traits, existing derangements, concept, narrative or social role, Jungian archetypes - essentially, Astral influences which would apply to them as a character. &quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:58:12-07:00","id":163924,"title":"","content":"Thanks; I thought it was an interesting avenue. I want to treat them as spirits of humanity, and that's an inherently weird thing for the Shadow. Blending it with the Astral and keeping my eyes on &quot;spirits Are their influences&quot; was my approach to that. I'll get to see how it works out mechanically and thematically over the next couple months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:13:37-07:00","id":164736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=163834#post163834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently storytelling werewolf, and have a player character which just became Purified. (That was a fun story to run on its own; she was a <i>Second Sight</i> shaman, and the cord that tethered her to her body was cut, so she discorporated; it's been a long, trying hike back from the spirit wilds, changing and being bound into webs of obligation as she goes. If there's a chance for it, I highly recommend role-playing out the experience.) Anyway, I did a full, personal write-up for the splat, which drew heavily on your work here, Octavo.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly speaking up because I also gave Purified access to influences, however I handled them rather differently. Since spirits <i>are </i>their influences, I gave them influences which relate to aspects of their psyche: virtue, vice, beliefs, personality traits, existing derangements, concept, narrative or social role, Jungian archetypes - essentially, Astral influences which would apply to them as a character. Picking up new influences from spirits would be hard (without becoming magath), but they are able to pick them up from ghosts and astral figments (or perhaps angels). I also decided that at Chi 7 (spirit rank 5), they can gain the influence &quot;Humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> My Purified character also has a warped ephemeral form - exaggerated by her influence dots - and a spirit name, both of which make her easy to mistake as an abstract spirit, for those who aren't already familiar with the rare choir of human spirits.<br /> <br /> I agree with quantumelody in how handle the &quot;downside&quot; to being Purified - that they are actually spirits now - but I didn't expand on that very much. In <i>Immortals</i>, it's explained that they get woven into the politics of the Shadow, in service to choirs and incarnae as a world-walking agent; that, along with the ordinary limitations that come with spirits, is all I have planned. But I do like the emphasis on new sensations, and growing disconnect to humanity as their new morality trait (on the other hand, that may be counterproductive with my assumptions that they are humanity spirits; then again, it could be a disconnect from their human life and a pull toward humanity in general . . . )<br /> <br /> I have the feeling the way I've written up Purified for my game is going to quickly lead to a over-powered character, to the point of only working well in mage chronicles. However, my game is nearly at 700 exp (pre-gmc system) so everything is kind of skewed in that direction . . .<br /> <br /> I rather like the Purified as a template, and expanding the rules for them is something I'm particularly interested in. I've enjoyed reading everyone else's approach to the subject quite a bit. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xc4XmROQ-hDKhsQdhrQWK5KpK-8OhlkFnrPcyTaUlgc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's my write-up</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this goes to show that given an initial condition and a final condition, there's enough in the WoD for people do do the intermediary steps in different ways! I'm really happy that resurrecting this thread has led to such awesome discussion.<br /> <br /> My decision to make the Influences more narrow exists because I think that it should be a limitation similar to the limitations of other spirits. Beyond the initial dots of Influence, I think that the only way of expanding one's repertoire should be through consuming spirits or harvesting a ton of Essence from a locus with those kinds of qualities, just like what spirits do to broaden their areas of Influence. We're approaching the psychology of the Purified in different ways (i.e., I don't consider them spirits of humanity), and this difference definitely shows in the thought processes we've had surrounding Influences! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do like the idea of having a Spirit name in Twilight and Shadow, and I will probably incorporate that.<br /> <br /> Through some conversations, I realized that I have a sentence in the document that should probably actually be its own section. My general assumption is that the ritual, poison experience, or quick, fast, and dirty version of the Purification Ritual create a mote of Essence that comes from both the ritual/suicide and the locus itself. The Essence is at high spin (after all, it has coalesced into a compact body from a dispersed area, much like a protoplanetary accretion disk) and on the exact spot where the Candidate is standing, so when the Candidate dies, their mind and soul are essentially ripped apart on the Shadow side where they are standing and infused into that mote of Essence. The spirit that comes out of it starts at Rank 2 because the Purification process and the meshing of the human soul into a mote of a lot of Essence as opposed to the tiny motes that birth regular spirits is a really powerful generator. The addition of the human soul and mind to the mix provides the spirit with a structural grounding (as the mind is reconstructed from the fragments and the soul parts absorbed; this is why Purified cannot be ghosts) and a fast tie to the dead body lying on the locus. At the end of the process, the creation of the Purified from the two components &quot;flings&quot; them from the locus to a random point in Shadow, and then the Purified has to walk back to the Shire.<br /> <br /> Question for you: Influences work in body in your case? How has that worked out in game play?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:16:05-07:00","id":164737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=163448#post163448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, that's lovely.Reading it through.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aww, no overhaul of the Siddhi? Half of them are part of the basic rules for interacting with Ephemeral beings now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that several of the Siddhi are useful. However, I think that most of them are just better off as the Numina that they're mimicking. Going through Siddhi wasn't in my original scope, but now I'm tempted to do so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:24:08-07:00","id":165081,"title":"","content":"I actually can't speak to that yet. The character hasn't made it back to her body yet; that'll actually be the upcoming session. Because the type of influences I'm using, they'll probably be rather strange to use, most often to manipulate the behavior of people around her.<br /> <br /> I can see good reasons for only allowing Influence use in their ephemeral form: typically being embodied gets in the way of a spirits powers, and it would encourage the player into twilight more often where they're perhaps more vulnerable. In the case of my particular player, I think it would just wind up with her rarely using the Influences though. Influences are very potent when they're used cleverly, but the descriptions are extremely vague in how they can be used to start with, they're a weird type of power to get a grasp on (except for mage veterans perhaps), and with influences related to human psyche using them gets even stranger. It could end up being super over-powered, particularly with how many influences I allow, but I'm hoping they'll be a nifty trick which rewards clever solutions and encourages stronger ties to human npcs - as well as stronger rivalries with spirits.<br /> <br /> As I find out the various complications and cool things from running Purified this way, I'll bring them up here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:49:06-07:00","id":165214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quantumelody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=164737#post164737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that several of the Siddhi are useful. However, I think that most of them are just better off as the Numina that they're mimicking. Going through Siddhi wasn't in my original scope, but now I'm tempted to do so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that, circa GMC...<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b> and <b>Warding</b> (actually, I misread Warding... I still think it needs to be overhauled. Because I am crazy.) are now essentially parts of the core rules for Spirits.<br /> <br /> Which, actually...<br /> <br /> Let me just do... this. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Siddhi of Summoning</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> Anyone may summon a Spirit, if they know the proper rituals. The Purified do not need to learn the proper rituals. Instead, the Siddhi of Summoning ensures that when they call, spirits answer. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Coming-and-Going Ways (Summoning </span></b>\u2022<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">)</span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 - 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Persuasion + Chi + Gauntlet Strength Modifier versus Resistance<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> <br /> One of the Purified may exceed the normal, mortal limits on summoning Spirits. The Purified may pay the cost of certain Manifestation conditions for a Spirit; this roll is only penalized if the Spirit does not wish to have their Manifestation conditions paid for. Coming-and-Going Ways may only be activated in an area with an Open condition corresponding to the Spirit they are attempting to bring forth.<br /> <br /> This Siddhi does not have to target a specific spirit; however, the Purified must specify at least which type of Spirit they wish to call forth, at which point this Siddhi's effects are applied to whatever corresponding spirit is closest.<br /> <br /> The Purified spends their chosen amount of Essence and then rolls:</div><div style=\"margin-left:80px\"><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Purified severely botches their invitation; the area they were trying to summon the spirit into loses the Open Condition.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Purified fails to draw the Spirit from Twilight.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The benefits of this Siddhi vary based on the amount of Essence spent on it:</div><ul><li><b>1 Essence:</b> The Purified either activates the Image Manifestation on behalf of the Spirit, or grants the spirit the Reaching condition.</li> <li><b>2 Essence:</b> The Purified activates the Fetter Manifestation on behalf of the Spirit, choosing which object or creature the Spirit becomes Fettered to.</li> <li><b>3 Essence:</b> The Purified activates the Materialize Manifestation on behalf of the Spirit.</li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:120px\">Each Manifestation or Condition uses the number of successes rolled for Coming-and-Going Ways for the purposes of determining how long they last.<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:80px\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> Extra successes are their own reward.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Summoning the Wandering Shade</b></span><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Summoning </span></b>\u2022\u2022<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">)</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <br /> While it is far more strenuous, Purified may extend the benefits of their sponsorship to Ghosts as well as spirits, tracing their will through the place in their soul where their Death should be.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Purified uses Coming-and-Going Ways, they may spend an additional point of Essence to affect a Ghost instead of a Spirit.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Calling Distant Names (Summoning \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cost: </span></b>1 Essence<br /> <br /> Of course, it is not truly summoning if you can only bring forth what is already there, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Whenever the Purified uses Coming-and-Going Ways, they may spend an additional point of Essence to have it summon a Spirit (or Ghost) from anywhere, regardless of distance. If the Purified's roll for Coming-and-Going Ways is successful, the Ephemeral being takes one turn to arrive at the Open Condition that the Purified is standing within, at which point the normal effects of a success for Coming-and-Going Ways take effect.<br /> <br /> Using Calling Distant Names applies the Mystical Connections modifier to the roll.</div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-11-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T03:09:16-07:00","id":165760,"title":"","content":"In my opinion the Summoning Siddhi from the book do not need any change. Your version only works at places where the Open Condition is already present, which means that the character sometime needs to do a lot of research and to laborous mortal rituals to create this condition. I do not really like this.<br /> <br /> I would just use the original version, with the addition that all levels generate the Open Condition (or at least the Resonant Condition).<br /> <br /> Enabling Manifestations also isn't really necessary I think. Purified can already see beings in Twilight, removing the need for the Image Manifestation. Granting Reaching does not make sense in terms of theme, especially as the spirit will come to you after the summoning, which means that Reaching is not necessary. Letting the spirit Materialize is already part of the original third power. The only manifestation that really misses in the original power set, is Fetter, but you could also have summoned a spirit with Fetter in the first place, if this is that important to you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do think your new version is nice and coherent, even if I think the changes are unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T04:07:38-07:00","id":165785,"title":"","content":"Image is so that <i>other</i> people can see your Spirit buddy.<br /> <br /> And part of the point is that the Spirit doesn't have to be willing for you to use your Siddhi on them; if you are enemies with Spirit Steve, you can summon him up, force him to Materialize, and then have some friends help you beat on him. Probably not lethal, granted, but enough to get your point across.<br /> <br /> And eh, I feel that doing the rituals feels more mystical. Still, I don't mind if you don't want to use my version; I just kinda have wanted to rewrite all the Siddhi for a while.<br /> (If you had the proper Mystical Connection, former Summoning 3 would let you summon the Idigam <i>from the moon, while they were still bound.</i> Also, the 3rd tier of the Siddhi says you can't use it on Ghosts? That's fine, <i>because it is already part of Summon the Wandering Shade</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T06:37:26-07:00","id":165861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=40168#post40168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Gifts from Werewolf: the Forsaken</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Gift Mechanics</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spirits generally grant their gifts to the Uratha, but some spirits can be convinced to teach them to respected Purified who provide them something of value in return. Purified cannot teach these to anyone unless they are projected into the Shadow with the \u201cSpirit Projection\u201d Siddhi. There, they are nearly indistinguishable from spirits, and can similarly teach these abilities to the Uratha or other Purified, provided something is provided in return. Gifts cost the same amount as Siddhi, but they are capped by the Purified\u2019s effective spirit rank (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Immortals</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> p 100). Use the activation dice pool listed in </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Werewolf: the Forsaken</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, but substitute the Purified\u2019s Chi in the place of the listed Renown trait. Gifts must be purchased in the order listed in </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Werewolf: the Forsaken</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, unless the player spends 1 extra experience. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Gift Lists</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Death </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Elemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Evasion</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Insight</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Inspiration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Knowledge</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Nature</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sharing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stealth</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Strength</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Technology</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Warding</span></span></span><br /> [COLOR=#000000][FONT=Arial][SIZE=15px]Weather</div> </div> </div> </div>Would they work with <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/gifts/\" target=\"_blank\">new Gifts organisation with Wolf, Moon and Shadow</a> ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T08:47:20-07:00","id":165963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=165785#post165785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Image is so that <i>other</i> people can see your Spirit buddy.<br /> <br /> And part of the point is that the Spirit doesn't have to be willing for you to use your Siddhi on them; if you are enemies with Spirit Steve, you can summon him up, force him to Materialize, and then have some friends help you beat on him. Probably not lethal, granted, but enough to get your point across.<br /> <br /> And eh, I feel that doing the rituals feels more mystical. Still, I don't mind if you don't want to use my version; I just kinda have wanted to rewrite all the Siddhi for a while.<br /> (If you had the proper Mystical Connection, former Summoning 3 would let you summon the Idigam <i>from the moon, while they were still bound.</i> Also, the 3rd tier of the Siddhi says you can't use it on Ghosts? That's fine, <i>because it is already part of Summon the Wandering Shade</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am ever going to use Siddhi, I'm probably going to tweak them. When that happens, I'll probably use your versions as inspiration for possible tweaks, so please keep them coming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:03:06-07:00","id":166065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=165861#post165861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would they work with <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/gifts/\" target=\"_blank\">new Gifts organisation with Wolf, Moon and Shadow</a> ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not certain about that. I'll probably revisit this question once I can leaf through the full pdf of Idigam Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T14:22:20-07:00","id":166225,"title":"","content":"Given the way the new gifts are meant to evoke and support The Hunt, I'm dubious about them working well for Purified. The Purified, I think, are interesting because they're basically playable spirits; as world-walkers they have a lot of influence over their environment if they play politics well enough, but they don't have the power to force change like mages, and aren't hunters or generally disliked as are Forsaken. Their powers should represent that niche - which I think a good number of the original gifts in forsaken do, but indigam is restructuring on 'the wolf must hunt'. Although, we'll see when a more complete gift list is out....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T14:40:13-07:00","id":166234,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm leaning towards new Gifts not working for Purified (my own 2 cents, as it were.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: I would totally rewrite the Siddhi to be based off the <i>actual</i> Hindu Siddhi, but shrinking to the size of an atom or taking any form might be a <i>tad</i> off-base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-11-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:40:40-07:00","id":166428,"title":"","content":"The comments people have had on the Doc so far have been superbly helpful (and the conversation here has been amazing, too). I've added a change log to the doc at the top. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fkn6_L9DjHEIhvx43uPDnQ9DE0DXd3HlINuJRnDc1zg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Re: Siddhi. I think that some of these can be mapped to Numina and replaced, but a few (i.e., shifting, warding) are things that have some nice touches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:04:47-07:00","id":179979,"title":"","content":"I've shifted around some of the Siddhi and expanded on Numina in the doc, if anyone is still following it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I condensed the Siddhi down and increased their Experience cost to reflect that they are a five-dot power that is much more useful than they were. Thoughts? <a href=\"http://bit.ly/1nthGj1\" target=\"_blank\">http://bit.ly/1nthGj1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","user":"quantumelody","date":". 06-25-2014, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T22:02:05-07:00","id":185362,"title":"","content":"In the nWoD Werewolf books and the spirit book it says to substitute Gifts as Numen if the Numen list does not cover what you need. After all the spirits are in essence teaching the Werewolves spirit powers.<br /> <br /> As far as the Purified, I think they would make a good write up for the new Werewolf book. The concept of the Purified is has many different forms of legends in many different cultures. Because Werewolves pretty much cover the spirit aspect of nWoD, it would be silly to write up a whole new book system for them. Though they very much need to be redone.<br /> <br /> Also giving them influences would be silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T17:55:23-07:00","id":185869,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to why you don't think Purified should gain Influences","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T18:39:52-07:00","id":185925,"title":"","content":"I also think it's good to keep in mind that they're connected to the Shadow, but not necessarily connected to Werewolves. It's similar to how a Mage or a Thaumaturge can be connected to the Underworld but aren't connected to Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T22:07:17-07:00","id":186030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=185869#post185869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to why you don't think Purified should gain Influences</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically it is OP. Story wise it actually doesn't make sense. It is like saying Werewolves should get influences because they are half spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=185925#post185925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think it's good to keep in mind that they're connected to the Shadow, but not necessarily connected to Werewolves. It's similar to how a Mage or a Thaumaturge can be connected to the Underworld but aren't connected to Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I fully understand. I just think it would be a good place to put them since spirits and the shadow will be heavily covered in that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T22:30:51-07:00","id":186043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=186030#post186030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically it is OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you actually understand what Influences do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T03:23:16-07:00","id":186154,"title":"","content":"You might be right about influences being OP. I haven't done any real play-testing with letting a player use them yet. I think it'll end up relying on the player using them, much like mage, but we'll see. I have to disagree about them not being appropriate for story reasons, though; Purified are humans which have become spirits. Their souls adapted to the shadow realm, and transformed into a spirit being; they merely inhabit their body. Or, at least, their relationship with their physical form is much more loose than werewolves, considering they leave it behind to cross worlds, can wander in a state of twilight, and continue as ephemeral beings once its slain. Half-spirit creatures are different from embodied spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T05:51:58-07:00","id":186215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=185362#post185362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the nWoD Werewolf books and the spirit book it says to substitute Gifts as Numen if the Numen list does not cover what you need. After all the spirits are in essence teaching the Werewolves spirit powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to let people know, Gifts and their Facets in the Idigam Chronicles, and the process of acquiring them, is explicitly not just teaching spirit powers. Gifts and Facets are very much tuned to werewolves and their nature, and Gifts are not lessons to be learned or magic incantations to be memorised. They inflict a more fundamental change than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the Purified, I think they would make a good write up for the new Werewolf book. The concept of the Purified is has many different forms of legends in many different cultures. Because Werewolves pretty much cover the spirit aspect of nWoD, it would be silly to write up a whole new book system for them. Though they very much need to be redone. </div> </div> </div>As far as I am aware, we're not putting Purified in the Idigam Chronicles - we have way too many other things that are central to the game line to put into the book, and even then we don't have the space to cram in everything we want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T18:28:03-07:00","id":186698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=186154#post186154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be right about influences being OP. \u200bI haven't done any real play-testing with letting a player use them yet. I think it'll end up relying on the player using them, much like mage, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Influences would be overpowered. In the port I did, they can only use Influences while projecting, not in their bodies. I think that this helps. The Purified already have a theme of &quot;outside of my fleshy safety blanket = dangerous.&quot; Being in an environment where they can use Influences would also open them up to (potentially) antagonistic or politically-charged interactions with other spirits looking to get Essence out of the same things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=186154#post186154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree about them not being appropriate for story reasons, though; Purified are humans which have become spirits. Their souls adapted to the shadow realm, and transformed into a spirit being; they merely inhabit their body. Or, at least, their relationship with their physical form is much more loose than werewolves, considering they leave it behind to cross worlds, can wander in a state of twilight, and continue as ephemeral beings once its slain. Half-spirit creatures are different from embodied spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Purified ritualistically hack immortality leveraging Shadow and end up turning themselves into Spirits. They are basically adept occultists' spirit echoes who have Claimed themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=186215#post186215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I am aware, we're not putting Purified in the Idigam Chronicles - we have way too many other things that are central to the game line to put into the book, and even then we don't have the space to cram in everything we want.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes perfect sense. They'd be much more appropriate in something like Book of Spirits as a PC-playable option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T19:22:59-07:00","id":186761,"title":"","content":"The issue I'm starting to have with Influences isn't that they are too powerful or too weak... It's that they had too little space dedicated to them.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not entirely sure of the big difference between Manipulate and Control (they are degrees of each-other), exactly what's appropriate mechanically with Strengthen, and of course why a whole Dot rating was wasted with a &quot;like the 4th dot, but <i>a lot of it</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is beyond the thematic issues of making, say, a Spirit of Destruction. It feels off to give them 4 dots of Influence (Destruction)...<br /> <br /> I guess I would have preferred a Blood Sorcery-esque approach, where you get 2 dots per Influence Dot to spread between a number of categories. That way I could have my Destruction spirit with their Destruction Influence getting split between Harm and Transformation, for example.<br /> <br /> An alternative would be to have different <i>kinds</i> of Influence, each with their own 5-step scale. So you could have a Destruction spirit with 2 dots sunk into Influence (Destruction)(Violent), which would be an Influence track set up around hurting things.<br /> <br /> Maybe combine the two approaches...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T19:31:27-07:00","id":186768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=186761#post186761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I'm starting to have with Influences isn't that they are too powerful or too weak... It's that they had too little space dedicated to them.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not entirely sure of the big difference between Manipulate and Control (they are degrees of each-other), exactly what's appropriate mechanically with Strengthen, and of course why a whole Dot rating was wasted with a &quot;like the 4th dot, but <i>a lot of it</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. They're pretty nebulous powers designed for storyteller characters, and I'm not sure I'd use them for player characters without a little tweaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T19:36:27-07:00","id":186770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=186761#post186761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I'm starting to have with Influences isn't that they are too powerful or too weak... It's that they had too little space dedicated to them.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not entirely sure of the big difference between Manipulate and Control (they are degrees of each-other), exactly what's appropriate mechanically with Strengthen, and of course why a whole Dot rating was wasted with a &quot;like the 4th dot, but <i>a lot of it</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is beyond the thematic issues of making, say, a Spirit of Destruction. It feels off to give them 4 dots of Influence (Destruction)...<br /> <br /> I guess I would have preferred a Blood Sorcery-esque approach, where you get 2 dots per Influence Dot to spread between a number of categories. That way I could have my Destruction spirit with their Destruction Influence getting split between Harm and Transformation, for example.<br /> <br /> An alternative would be to have different <i>kinds</i> of Influence, each with their own 5-step scale. So you could have a Destruction spirit with 2 dots sunk into Influence (Destruction)(Violent), which would be an Influence track set up around hurting things.<br /> <br /> Maybe combine the two approaches...</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember a section of a book in which there was a discussion of a dog-spirit having Influence (Loyalty) and Influence (Dogs) at the same time as a reflection of the type of dog-spirit it is. As spirits become more complex (i.e., Rank 3+) they tend to have much more complicated facets due to the type of Essence they have been consuming. So, if it's a Rank 4 Spirit of Destruction, it could very well have something like Influence (Impulsiveness), Influence (Chaos), and Influence (Destruction). Or ... Influence (Destruction) and Influence (Entropy). Just as examples. It was my understanding that the Influence scale mechanics worked exactly like your description ... you have a base number to distribute around to different things, but the Influences are each tracked separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T14:09:08-07:00","id":187397,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I'm just not too sure what Influence (Weakness) would <i>strengthen</i>, to be perfectly fair.<br /> <br /> And I remember that section too; I'm just not sure if that's <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm looking at it from the point of view of &quot;I want to do a Mage Light where instead of the Arcana, you buy dots in Influence (Forces), Influence (Mind), etc, etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another alternative idea was handing out Dread Power dots as part of influences and doing away with Numina, using the Influences to calculate the effects of the Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T18:15:03-07:00","id":187557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=187397#post187397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I'm just not too sure what Influence (Weakness) would <i>strengthen</i>, to be perfectly fair.<br /> <br /> And I remember that section too; I'm just not sure if that's <i>enough</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would probably have the same exact effects as Strengthen, but in the opposite direction -- i.e., decreasing Structure in an object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:25:49-07:00","id":195038,"title":"","content":"Influence (Weapons), perhaps? Dealing damage seems more the province of Numen, like Blast.<br /> <br /> However, am I reading this right? Purified gain Chi, Rank, and Influence without spending XP? If I'm not misunderstanding, that seems strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T11:46:44-07:00","id":195639,"title":"","content":"The thing is, I don't really like Numen as a post-GMC thing, ya know?<br /> <br /> I mean, we pretty much have them as a Legacy thing; in nWoD, we have Aspects, Dread Powers, and Numina. From some of the spoilers I've seen, Aspects are going to be folded into Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> Which leads me to ask: why even keep Numina as a thing? Why not fold <i>everything</i> into Dread Powers, and leave Influences as the &quot;unique powers&quot; of Ephemeral Beings? Just let them spend Essence to power Dread Powers, and we're set.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring up a Spirit of Destruction is that Influences as written are inherently a <i>constructive</i> thing; you build up whatever you have influence over. Why can't I have a Spirit of Happiness suck up someone's happiness entirely, removing the Resonant condition but getting a big boost of Essence? Why can't my Spirit of Birds use their Influence to weaken other Spirits of Birds, so as to better eat up their tasty, tasty Essence?<br /> <br /> When it comes down to it, my ideal Ephemeral Beings rules would boil down to &quot;assign their Influences and Attributes, and then we're done.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T11:50:26-07:00","id":195642,"title":"","content":"Well, the first reason I see for the separation is that a Numen is a single power without a dot rating, while Dread Powers using dot ratings. I think that's a distinction to keep in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T11:30:46-07:00","id":196491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=195639#post195639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TWhy can't I have a Spirit of Happiness suck up someone's happiness entirely, removing the Resonant condition but getting a big boost of Essence? Why can't my Spirit of Birds use their Influence to weaken other Spirits of Birds, so as to better eat up their tasty, tasty Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, in fact, a Numen that allows you to steal Willpower and Essence from targets.<br /> <br /> I'm not sue why you want this power to be an Influence specifically. It seems like stripping out everything but Attributes and Influences would either involve removing all the iconic abilities of Spirits or reinventing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T19:17:23-07:00","id":196637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=195038#post195038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influence (Weapons), perhaps? Dealing damage seems more the province of Numen, like Blast.<br /> <br /> However, am I reading this right? Purified gain Chi, Rank, and Influence without spending XP? If I'm not misunderstanding, that seems strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purified start at Chi 1. They have to buy all levels higher than that. Purified Chi already has a correspondence with Spirit Rank in the core text. You can derive the number of Influences from their Spirit Rank ... so Chi is a cascading reaction. To have EXTRA Influence dots requires purchasing the Greater Influence Numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:24:40-07:00","id":207920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=195639#post195639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I bring up a Spirit of Destruction is that Influences as written are inherently a <i>constructive</i> thing; you build up whatever you have influence over.</div> </div> </div> </div>From whence sprung this spirit of Destruction?<br /> <br /> Spirits don't emerge from a vacuum and destroying/sacrificing instances of their purviews is specifically called out as a means of <i>feeding</i> most spirits on account of it having good odds of orphaning a spirit that's suitable for consumption by the beneficiary.<br /> <br /> Spirits are stories. Spirits are consequences. Why should a spirit of Destruction arise instead of, say, <i>literally any other kind of spirit with a destructive bent?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T11:24:43-07:00","id":209435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quantumelody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=196637#post196637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purified start at Chi 1. They have to buy all levels higher than that. Purified Chi already has a correspondence with Spirit Rank in the core text. You can derive the number of Influences from their Spirit Rank ... so Chi is a cascading reaction. To have EXTRA Influence dots requires purchasing the Greater Influence Numen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, OK, I partly misinterpreted. It does seem a little too cheap to be giving away Influences (BTW, why Influences and not Numina, Attributes, etc?)<br /> <br /> But I thought you didn't actually need to buy Chi <i>at all</i>, it just rose naturally. That it was completely decoupled from the existing XP mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should a spirit of Destruction arise instead of, say, <i>literally any other kind of spirit with a destructive bent?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would <i>assume</i> it fed on Essence that was particularly resonant with destruction; and eventually grew into a spirit of destruction, with a bent towards particular kinds of destruction.<br /> <br /> Is there some reason a spirit with a destructive purview would be such a strange idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:08:02-07:00","id":209516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=209435#post209435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would <i>assume</i> it fed on Essence that was particularly resonant with destruction; and eventually grew into a spirit of destruction, with a bent towards particular kinds of destruction.<br /> <br /> Is there some reason a spirit with a destructive purview would be such a strange idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>For roughly the same reason that &quot;Influence: Anchor&quot; is uselessly nonspecific and recursive as a means of delineating ghost-Influences.<br /> <br /> <i>It's not actually a thing that you can concretely encounter.</i><br /> <br /> You don't get spirits of destruction arising from acts of destruction; there's more concrete phenomena front and center that form the backbone of these particular destructive spirits, and if those spirits diversify their portfolios along the axis of &quot;destructive phenomena&quot; then they become known as spirits of destruction. That reputation doesn't change the fact that there will be methods of summoning them that actually allow them to stay in the world of flesh for more than the length of a sustained demolition.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spirits of destruction&quot; tend to have Influences that resonate with either the <i>processes</i> or the <i>products</i> of destruction, and the latter, from context, tend to be incredibly bad-news in the first place; the predatory animistic spirit of a <i>dead or destroyed</i> thing - and here I remind you that animism means &quot;everything is alive&quot; - is not an ordinary spirit that will only fuck up its surroundings as much as any other unmonitored spirit. It is a Thing That Should Not Be - there's magath mentioned in the books that arose from the stacks of corpses that the Mongol Hordes left in their wake.<br /> <br /> For run-of-the-mill fuck-shit-up &quot;destructive spirits&quot; you call on storm-spirits, foul-tempered elementals, reflections of nature's fury or technology's caprice, manifestations of the aggregate resonance of The Great Equalizer. You don't dick around with trying to find spirits that have hung their hat on a universal force to do a job any spirit with a body and a bad attitude can pull off.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say:<br /> <br /> &quot;Destructive purview&quot; is manageable without putting &quot;Purview: Destruction&quot; on the thing's character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T17:09:25-07:00","id":212944,"title":"","content":"Isn't one of the example rites one where you can rewrite a Locus to match an Influence of your devising? It might be hard, but you might <i>eventually</i> get just the right balance to build up &quot;pure&quot; &quot;Destruction&quot; Essence.<br /> <br /> Maybe Destruction was a poor choice. What about a Spirit of, say, Drowning? What would they &quot;strengthen&quot;? The viscosity of water forcing itself into your lungs? Maybe the strength of currents (but that would be an Influence over water...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T19:12:41-07:00","id":213053,"title":"","content":"The rite requires you to have symbolic components that evoke the target resonance. <i>T</i><i>here are more useful resonances to aim for.</i><br /> <br /> Again: &quot;spirit of ___&quot; does not necessitate &quot;Influence: ___&quot; and it's a gross error to make that assumption. There's Helions with no Sunlight Influence. There's no spirits of drowning. That's geists. There's spirits of <i>watery death</i>.<br /> <br /> Think of Influences as <i>what lets the spirit stay on Earth</i> before you think of them as a powerset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T17:21:31-08:00","id":351069,"title":"","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> So, callishka and I have been working a bit more on the mods I mentioned a few pages ago. We have greatly expanded them into a 75-page document containing a reworking of Siddhi/Numina, Merits, Integrity, and a whole host of other options that may be of interest to others. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3MlzBp3QvDlcVk0TFhwcW1PRHc/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3M...ew?usp=sharing</a>.<br /> <br /> Happy New Year!<br /> <br /> - Kaye","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T23:45:28-08:00","id":351398,"title":"","content":"I'm reading it right now, and enjoying it, though the PDF's formatting has a bunch of blank pages that are weird.<br /> <br /> I noticed this section: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Purified can respond to the one-dot, rolless activated powers (i.e., a<br /> <br /> Vampire\u2019s Majesty) by rolling Composure + Chi. The same change that<br /> <br /> makes their blood alien and inedible gives them a natural resistance<br /> <br /> to powers meant to control the human herd. (This, incidentally, is<br /> <br /> one of the reasons Purified are commonly called \u201dopt-outs\u201d \u2014 the<br /> <br /> slur originates from how disconnected they are from the food chain.) </div> </div> </div>and while I haven't seen any Predatory Aura/Hunter's Aspect/Nimbus-like mechanics yet, those are the things used to contest this sort of stuff. Maybe one might be applicable here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T02:47:55-08:00","id":351474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=351398#post351398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading it right now, and enjoying it, though the PDF's formatting has a bunch of blank pages that are weird.<br /> <br /> I noticed this section:<br /> <br /> and while I haven't seen any Predatory Aura/Hunter's Aspect/Nimbus-like mechanics yet, those are the things used to contest this sort of stuff. Maybe one might be applicable here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Leetsepeak, thanks for giving feedback. I think the blank pages are because the style of the document is like a book? quantumelody can speak to that.<br /> <br /> As for the second point, if I understand correctly, isn't that what rolling Comp + Chi accomplishes? Kindred roll a Power State + BA, for instance. Or are you suggesting that Purified should have an aura of weirdness that other supes can pick up on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T04:54:22-08:00","id":351508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=351474#post351474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leetsepeak, thanks for giving feedback. I think the blank pages are because the style of the document is like a book? quantumelody can speak to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. In the documentation for classicthesis, it mentions that there is a problem that can happen in pdfs for the table of contents, so we're using \\cleardoublepage as suggested. It's not as simple as skipping pages, though --- it forces the chapters to begin on odd pages. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=351398#post351398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and while I haven't seen any Predatory Aura/Hunter's Aspect/Nimbus-like mechanics yet, those are the things used to contest this sort of stuff. Maybe one might be applicable here?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if the Artifice mechanic is used, this is easy because there is secretly a creepy hungry spirit thing shifting beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> In the original <i>Immortals</i> text, it says that Purified do not have edible blood. (They're like fishing bycatch in some ways for the frustrated Daeva who is just trying to make everyone like him so he can get some Vitae.) Without the Artifice, half of the roll justification comes from this thematic choice: They're not food. The other half comes from the fact that even if they don't have Predatory Auras, Purified are spirit zombies Claiming their special spirit-resurrected bodies. (See Simulacrum, Chi Bleeds, &amp;c.) They're not even remotely human any longer, and it's pine cones all the way down. ;D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T09:52:25-08:00","id":351767,"title":"","content":"Also, to clarify the above with minimal mobile typos, Purified bodies are already protective because the spirit-soul can only be attacked and temporarily or permanently destroyed while projected out of it. So they have that spirit-person core inside of a fleshy safe house. It's why I said detecting an embodied Purified's rank or that they are something filled with Essence is a roll. The roll to lash out is also related to the body's safety.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, projected Purified should totally and unabashedly register as spirits. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T09:56:46-08:00","id":351771,"title":"","content":"Comp + Chi accomplishes the same goal, it just doesn't <i>do </i>anything, which is my only issue with it. Werewolves and Mages aren't strictly human, so they can contest predatory auras with their Nimbus or Hunter's Aspect. It's not just that these things are dicepools, it's that they both inflict interesting effects in their own right. What I'm saying is that perhaps instead of just being able to resist other Auras, that it might be cool if the Purified had an Aura mechanic as well. Perhaps something that reflects their Spirit nature? Maybe something based on their Influences? They're a fun innate Template ability that all the splats are getting in the 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T10:10:33-08:00","id":351775,"title":"","content":"It's a compelling idea, but then if they had such an aura, it would suggest that other supernaturals can detect them automatically, since that is one of the effects of having a supernatural aura. This long-range detection goes against the idea that purified are spirits hiding inside bodies. We are interpreting purified as being &quot;Not on the radar&quot;. If they were on the radar, other supernaturals would have learned about them easily over the years, including Uratha, Who are typically not keen on &quot;Claimed&quot; creatures walking the streets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T12:10:23-08:00","id":351893,"title":"","content":"You've definitely put a lot of work into the mods, and some of the ideas are actually quite interesting (like giving them Influences or treating them as spirits with simplified attributes when out of their bodies), but I personally <i>really don't like </i>the &quot;Purified are essentially spirits&quot; thing and a lot of the nitty gritty details that come with that implication or you gave them alongside it.<br /> <br /> A few things also seem like overcomplicating matters and giving them more power that they don't really need, like extending Chi to 10 and their means of resisting 1 dot powers (they already have Chi, why not simply use Supernatural Tolerance as usual or the Clash Of Wills mechanic?).<br /> <br /> Kudos for the effort though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T13:37:23-08:00","id":351937,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kudos!<br /> <br /> It seems like you and we have a basic disagreement about the direction to take Purified in, based on the suggestions provided by the core Immortals text. That's a shame, but I hope it gives you some ideas and mechanics to try out. Use the lineages, merits, and conditions anyway, maybe.<br /> <br /> One comment about your other point: 1 Dot powers in GMC/WoD 2e are rather different than they were in 1e, and Clash of Wills is when two powers clash, which is not what's going on with 1 Dot powers in 2e.<br /> <br /> Again, thanks for taking a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T14:13:11-08:00","id":351969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=351893#post351893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've definitely put a lot of work into the mods, and some of the ideas are actually quite interesting (like giving them Influences or treating them as spirits with simplified attributes when out of their bodies), but I personally <i>really don't like </i>the &amp;quot;Purified are essentially spirits&amp;quot; thing and a lot of the nitty gritty details that come with that implication or you gave them alongside it.<br /> <br /> A few things also seem like overcomplicating matters and giving them more power that they don't really need, like extending Chi to 10 and their means of resisting 1 dot powers (they already have Chi, why not simply use Supernatural Tolerance as usual or the Clash Of Wills mechanic?).<br /> <br /> Kudos for the effort though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any other thoughts on the Purified about other ways to interpret them? It's always interesting to hear that sort of stuff. I like the groundwork for this PDF'd version while other things give me some misgivings. More ideas are always good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T18:06:24-08:00","id":352139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=351775#post351775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a compelling idea, but then if they had such an aura, it would suggest that other supernaturals can detect them automatically, since that is one of the effects of having a supernatural aura. This long-range detection goes against the idea that purified are spirits hiding inside bodies. We are interpreting purified as being &quot;Not on the radar&quot;. If they were on the radar, other supernaturals would have learned about them easily over the years, including Uratha, Who are typically not keen on &quot;Claimed&quot; creatures walking the streets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Predatory Auras are passively detected by other Kindred, but the same doesn't hold true for all auras. Mages can only see other Mages Nimbus auras when they're scrutinizing it deeply with Mage Sight or when those Mages cast spells, but it doesn't passively indicate to anybody watching that they're Supernatural.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is full of plenty of weird things that defy easy classification, so provided the Aura response that they can choose to use is unique to the Purified rather than a universal element of Spirits, it defies easy classification as a Spirit.<br /> <br /> Another thing I've observed: In the section about auras, it's still using that color code system, when that sort of thing seems to have been dropped in the 2nd edition. Nothing is necessarily broken by using it, but it's worth noting that someone using, say, Auspex, isn't looking at your emotional swatches, they're asking the questions offered by Auspex's discipline dots, which DOES include asking &quot;Is this a supernatural creature?&quot;<br /> <br /> Thusfar it seems like Demons are the only ones with an ability to reflexively spoof that sort of thing, so maybe the Purified practice some active form of concealment, rather than simply assuming they passively deceive everything around them. There doesn't seem to be much in the template about them <i>hiding </i>as Spirits in bodies, more <i>being </i>Spirits in bodies, which is, IMO, an important semantical difference.<br /> <br /> If Werewolves don't know much about them, it's because they don't know much about anything that falls outside their direct area of expertise. The assumption is that they're not walking around with a treasure trove of lore for Kindred or Mages or Sin-Eaters either, and you could argue those all do much less work to conceal themselves from Werewolves. I think this assumption is pretty valid when it comes to Purified as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T21:43:38-08:00","id":352323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=351969#post351969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any other thoughts on the Purified about other ways to interpret them? It's always interesting to hear that sort of stuff. I like the groundwork for this PDF'd version while other things give me some misgivings. More ideas are always good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my problem with that take on them is that it completely removes most of the ambiguity and doubt that comes with the question of <i>what the Purified are</i>. By just outright saying &quot;they're spirits/they've become special spirits&quot;. Comparing them to Claimed who have permanently fixed themselves to their original body also rubs me the wrong way, since even special snowflake ones shouldn't work like that. They don't get to just reform their original host body from nothing. Like Purified can.<br /> <br /> I also always thought of their Morality/Integrity as also marking how far from slipping into the spirit side of things they are - an additional indicator of the proximity of their minds to animist ephemeral beings. Because, relevant, Spirits do not in fact have an Integrity equivalent, so a Purified's Integrity falling to 0 could very well mean the same to them as losing human-like mentality entirely in favor of a spirit-like one.<br /> <br /> (Though, as a friend pointed out to me, once Werewolf comes out with its 2e, they might benefit more from a modified Harmony.)<br /> <br /> But without wanting to go on a huge tangent and lacking the brain fuel to go into an extended argument over it at this time, that conflict (their bodies and souls become closer to spirits', but how closer?) and how their unique natures can toss them into the middle of many situations involving ephemeral entities and other long lasting supernaturals, are very important parts of the Purified to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of mechanics, giving them Influences sounds like a doable thing, but I'd actually take more from Bailey's Kigan (because I love the hell out of it and a few things there are ridiculously suited for this) than anything else. Essentially, import the Spirit Court merit covering the favor they can acquire with a specific court, and then allow them to purchase dots of its Influence no greater than the merit rating. As they aren't actually true spirits (even if becoming Purified most definitely makes them closer, and they aren't plain humans anymore spiritually speaking), they'd require a sucess on a roll to succeed on using Influence, with successes equal to damage if used for those purposes.<br /> <br /> As for their projected ephemeral forms, I like the idea of using the simplified attributes. But with the average of each attribute category to determine Power, Finesse and Resistance instead of adding them (capped by whatever), while they retain their skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:36:22-08:00","id":352613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352323#post352323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of my problem with that take on them is that it completely removes most of the ambiguity and doubt that comes with the question of <i>what the Purified are</i>. By just outright saying &quot;they're spirits/they've become special spirits&quot;. Comparing them to Claimed who have permanently fixed themselves to their original body also rubs me the wrong way, since even special snowflake ones shouldn't work like that. They don't get to just reform their original host body from nothing. Like Purified can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't actually read that as ambiguity in the core text. I can see a Purified not actually knowing what they have done to themselves (and I think that's what the shoulder-shrug intended to capture, not that they <i>hadn't</i> turned themselves into spirits). Claimed are similar and yet different: They're people who have a spirit that fuses into them. Purified do a ritual, and there is no spirit middleman in this relationship.<br /> <br /> And yes -- Purified have a Morality trait. That's a huge difference between them and natural spirits. It makes it easier for them to walk around in states of self-denial about what they actually are &amp;c.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352323#post352323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of mechanics, giving them Influences sounds like a doable thing, but I'd actually take more from Bailey's Kigan (because I love the hell out of it and a few things there are ridiculously suited for this) than anything else. Essentially, import the Spirit Court merit covering the favor they can acquire with a specific court, and then allow them to purchase dots of its Influence no greater than the merit rating. As they aren't actually true spirits (even if becoming Purified most definitely makes them closer, and they aren't plain humans anymore spiritually speaking), they'd require a sucess on a roll to succeed on using Influence, with successes equal to damage if used for those purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about the same Influence mechanic, right? Influences are something that is intrinsic to a spirit. It's related to how much Essence with a relevant resonance they eat so that they can go up in Spirit Rank and gain more Influences. As they become more powerful, they're more capable of sophisticated thought and plotting surrounding how they are going to get their Essence fix and protect what they have from other spirits. That's an interesting idea, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352323#post352323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for their projected ephemeral forms, I like the idea of using the simplified attributes. But with the average of each attribute category to determine Power, Finesse and Resistance instead of adding them (capped by whatever), while they retain their skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen other modifications that skim the top attribute, and that's how this one originally went, too. I decided that, given Rank, they needed to have higher P, F, R stats just due to the intersupe dynamics in Shadow. They will never be as powerful as extremely powerful spirits even with this, but they do stand a chance --- and I think it represents in some ways that their spirit cores are not throttled by being encased in a body.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:40:49-08:00","id":352616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352139#post352139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another thing I've observed: In the section about auras, it's still using that color code system, when that sort of thing seems to have been dropped in the 2nd edition. Nothing is necessarily broken by using it, but it's worth noting that someone using, say, Auspex, isn't looking at your emotional swatches, they're asking the questions offered by Auspex's discipline dots, which DOES include asking &quot;Is this a supernatural creature?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. I still like the idea of what their auras look like because it relates to some ideas about how the Purification process would actually look to a Shadow observer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352139#post352139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thusfar it seems like Demons are the only ones with an ability to reflexively spoof that sort of thing, so maybe the Purified practice some active form of concealment, rather than simply assuming they passively deceive everything around them. There doesn't seem to be much in the template about them <i>hiding </i>as Spirits in bodies, more <i>being </i>Spirits in bodies, which is, IMO, an important semantical difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of active concealment do you think would be appropriate?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T09:28:18-08:00","id":352763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352323#post352323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of my problem with that take on them is that it completely removes most of the ambiguity and doubt that comes with the question of <i>what the Purified are</i>. By just outright saying &quot;they're spirits/they've become special spirits&quot;. Comparing them to Claimed who have permanently fixed themselves to their original body also rubs me the wrong way, since even special snowflake ones shouldn't work like that. They don't get to just reform their original host body from nothing. Like Purified can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it removes this doubt from players and places it squarely on the character/drama side. The ambiguity you're referring to is, IMO, largely an artifact of space-saving efforts by the writers, who seem to have intended Purified to be very spirit-like and to grow even more spirit-like over time. Our mod does something very WoDish, we think, which is to give characters an identity and motivation problem: they may think and feel that they are immortal humans, but they are not human anymore--or only echoes of human in a spirit of something primal. Slowly getting glimpses of just how alien they have become and having to contend with increasingly intrusive urges is compelling, to me. I'm not sure exactly what the draw is of making Purified ambiguous to the players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also always thought of their Morality/Integrity as also marking how far from slipping into the spirit side of things they are - an additional indicator of the proximity of their minds to animist ephemeral beings. Because, relevant, Spirits do not in fact have an Integrity equivalent, so a Purified's Integrity falling to 0 could very well mean the same to them as losing human-like mentality entirely in favor of a spirit-like one.<br /> <br /> But without wanting to go on a huge tangent and lacking the brain fuel to go into an extended argument over it at this time, that conflict (their bodies and souls become closer to spirits', but how closer?) and how their unique natures can toss them into the middle of many situations involving ephemeral entities and other long lasting supernaturals, are very important parts of the Purified to me. </div> </div> </div>You seem to have just described the very morality system used in our mod, only from the perspective of things that are humanish and become something more spiritish over time. Ours takes the premise that the morality is a mimicry that protects Purified in their interactions on the material side, much like Humanity protects the undead. In fact--and Kaye may have a better understanding about this since she wrote this part--Simulacrum is rather like Humanity: a memory or echo of how humans behave that helps the creature pass in public. The shock a character can experience is to notice that they aren't what they think they are, and that their humanity may only be a mental projection or a habit gradually being challenged by their hunger for Essence. It turns out there's a cost to making yourself eternally young and storing your entire soul not as flesh (which, after all, can now be endlessly regrown, brain and bone), but as ephemera of a certain resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T09:53:58-08:00","id":352782,"title":"","content":"[Cont.]<br /> <br /> I think that my last line is a keystone for me: It turns out there's a cost to making yourself eternally young and storing your entire soul not as flesh (which, after all, can now be endlessly regrown, brain and bone), but as ephemera of a certain resonance. Like, occultist, did you really think that you could kill yourself on a locus, make it so that your body can be endlessly resurrected even from a pinch of your dust, and still be a human?<br /> <br /> Obviously your soul has to have gone somewhere \u2013 it has to have become something. You can't do something that drastic and stay what you are. It's like a math problem: things have to equal each other on both sides. If you become deathless on one side, the material side, it's because you have completely removed everything that pins you to that side, using ritualistic death on an anchor between the two realms. But it also means that you are now pinned to the other side, the Shadow side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T10:55:34-08:00","id":352876,"title":"","content":"One more post before I forget. Your comments have been very thought-provoking, and I appreciate them. They are helping me figure out the philosophy underpinning this mod, and how it differs from other people's interpretations.<br /> <br /> I have a question. If purified are not ultimately spirits, then how can they be nearly destroyed in spirit form, reduced to tiny motes of essence, regrow themselves in spirit form, and then resurrect their fleshly bodies? What is that little mote? Why is it that removing its last bit of the essence and destroying it will kill it just as one kills a spirit, if they are not actually spirits? When that little nearly destroyed mote grows a little bit, regaining some sentience, what is it? Can it truly be referred to as a human spirit hybrid? It is barely conscious, its body is ash in some Hunter's crematory oven or soggy bones at the bottom of the ocean, and it will be a while before it has enough essence to knit its body back together and repossess it. During all that time, what is this creature? We take the stance that it is almost entirely spirit, and that it has been a spirit since the moment the ritual succeeded, even if the ritualist did not actually understand what it had become.<br /> <br /> If it is not a spirit, why does it adhere to the most fundamental spirit metaphysics, but utterly ignores human physics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 12-28-2014, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T12:05:20-08:00","id":352950,"title":"","content":"They can already have a motivation and identity problem without outright stating what becoming a Purified did to them. I would not find Kindred nearly as interesting if the presence of the Beast and their relation to the Strix was explained. Both approaches may be valid, but I don't think the writers intended for us to interpret that as the Purified literally becoming spirits. They alter their souls to become more like spirits: right there there's already a wide breadth of possible conflict to explore. Removing the ambiguity, in my opinion, is not going to add anything to the storytelling - it's just shrinking what it offers.<br /> <br /> No, Integrity as I see it being used for the purified has different paradigms from the morality used in the mod (that you've in fact already pointed out). I don't appreciate the premise of Simulacrum as a &quot;mimicry&quot; of human behavior because it jumps from the proposition that Purified are spirits at their core by default, which I do not believe was the intent of the writers. It's another unnecessary thing from a possibly fallacious assumption that just overcomplicates them far as I'm concerned, because Integrity with logical caveats is enough. Calling Humanity just a &quot;mimicry of how Humans behave&quot; for Vampires is also grossly simplifying it.<br /> <br /> And even for those Purified with high Integrity that do not dabble much in the spirit world, the subject of what they are and what they have become will never cease being relevant. In fact, it should logically only grow more relevant with age. The doubt might not be that dissimilar from Slashers and Hunters with increasing number of Endowments. As well, because Purified are spiritually different from regular humans, does not make necessarily make them different mentally.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think we'll disagree because we don't look at the Purified from the same points of view. I will say the following: I respect the work you've put into this mod, and I acknowledge your effort. But personally, and subjectively, I do not agree with how it goes about them.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Because the ritual that makes them Purified alters their spiritual nature. They might certainly not be regular humans, but that alone does not make them true spirits, and they most certainly keep human mentalities, even if they now have to deal with a whole new host of things that human minds usually do not have to. (Again, because they become more like spirits does not make them spirits.) It's worth nothing ghosts also work on several of the same metaphysics, and even regular humans can leave ghosts behind following their deaths. And funnily enough, death is an important lynchpin in the rite to become a Purified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-28-2014, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T12:06:04-08:00","id":352951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quantumelody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352616#post352616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point. I still like the idea of what their auras look like because it relates to some ideas about how the Purification process would actually look to a Shadow observer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What kind of active concealment do you think would be appropriate?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I need to finish reading your powers section, but something like the Mortal Mask Numen, either as a raw Numina they can take or in some altered form suited to their nature. Mortal Mask allows people to tell by making a Wits + Composure roll - Finesse, but I think if the Purified had a trick like it, it'd work better on account of having actual bodies. It could conceal Artifice Breaks maybe, on top of invoking a clash of wills with anything trying to tell if they're not human, possibly using Composure + Chi as its dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T14:28:58-08:00","id":353139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352950#post352950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I think we'll disagree because we don't look at the Purified from the same points of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's pretty clear that that's the case. Thanks for taking a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:38:01-08:00","id":358404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=352951#post352951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need to finish reading your powers section, but something like the Mortal Mask Numen, either as a raw Numina they can take or in some altered form suited to their nature. Mortal Mask allows people to tell by making a Wits + Composure roll - Finesse, but I think if the Purified had a trick like it, it'd work better on account of having actual bodies. It could conceal Artifice Breaks maybe, on top of invoking a clash of wills with anything trying to tell if they're not human, possibly using Composure + Chi as its dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am thinking about phrasing for mechanical elegance (and thematic integration). I think that making this an innate quality makes sense. One of the reasons for making Projection an innate quality is that everyone has to buy it, and it's not like it's a tangible artifact like a Touchstone or a Haven or something. A Morphic Aura (not Predatory Aura) should also be innate if everyone playing a Purified would need it. I've integrated the small piece about sensing other Purified through physical touch. I based this on Simulacrum to reflect that Simulacrum is related to how easily they can pass and simulate human Integrity.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Morphic Aura</b><br /> <br /> Purified exhibit an aura that many other supernatural beings can pick up on, but while in their physical bodies, their spirit nature attempts to conceal itself from other supernatural types. Other supernaturals may make a <i>Wits + Composure</i> roll penalized by the Purified's Simulacrum/Integrity to see through their human shell and register them as something different or noteworthy. Note that while Projected in Twilight or Shadow, there can be no attempt at concealment. <br /> <br /> With Purified and embodied Spirits, the situation is different: Any Purified can sense a connection to Shadow and relative Chi with an unpenalized <i>Intelligence + Occult</i> roll, performed reflexively with skin-to-skin contact.<br /> <br /> <i>Buttressing: </i>Purified spirit natures will recoil in response to Lashing Out, the one-dot Disciplines Awe and Dread Presence, and other powers that allow for a Predatory Aura-based resistance automatically. Not doing so requires the expenditure of 1 Willpower point. The resistance is based on <i>Composure + Chi</i>. If resisting Lashing Out, Purified cannot impose Conditions, but they may receive the Conditions Showing or Threatened (as appropriate) if they fail their defensive roll.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:45:06-08:00","id":358407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quantumelody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=358404#post358404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am thinking about phrasing for mechanical elegance (and thematic integration). I think that making this an innate quality makes sense. One of the reasons for making Projection an innate quality is that everyone has to buy it, and it's not like it's a tangible artifact like a Touchstone or a Haven or something. A Morphic Aura (not Predatory Aura) should also be innate if everyone playing a Purified would need it. I've integrated the small piece about sensing other Purified through physical touch. I based this on Simulacrum to reflect that Simulacrum is related to how easily they can pass and simulate human Integrity.[INDENT]<b>Morphic Aura</b><br /> <br /> Purified exhibit an aura that many other supernatural beings can pick up on, but while in their physical bodies, their spirit nature attempts to conceal itself from other supernatural types. Other supernaturals may make a <i>Wits + Composure</i> roll penalized by the Purified's Simulacrum/Integrity to see through their human shell and register them as something different or noteworthy. Note that while Projected in Twilight or Shadow, there can be no attempt at concealment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be going too far with this particular part. Barring Vampires with other Vampires, we haven't actually seen anything that indicates supernaturals sense eachother's auras, merely that they can contest one another's auras with them. Vampires detect Vampires automatically because of theirs, but Mages require Mage Sight scrutiny and whatnot. Basically, you don't need to put this in terms of Wits + Composure, because sensing whether they're a supernatural being or not is <i>always </i>more involved than a simple Perception roll. I suggest just saying that anyone attempting to discern their nature suffers a penalty to the roll equal to their Simulacrum score. It covers messing with Mage Sight that way, or Auspex, or whatever Gifts Werewolves might bring, etcetera.<br /> <br /> Nobody senses supernatural nature through a Wits + Composure roll, that its used with Mortal Mask represents that there can/should be something wrong with an Ephemeral Being's imperfect mortal guise that even a mundane mortal can notice. Notably, mortals can't automatically tell if you're a Werewolf, a Mage or a Vampire through JUST a Wits + Composure roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:47:13-08:00","id":358408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=358407#post358407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might be going too far with this particular part. Barring Vampires with other Vampires, we haven't actually seen anything that indicates supernaturals sense eachother's auras, merely that they can contest one another's auras with them. Vampires detect Vampires automatically because of theirs, but Mages require Mage Sight scrutiny and whatnot. Basically, you don't need to put this in terms of Wits + Composure, because sensing whether they're a supernatural being or not is <i>always </i>more involved than a simple Perception roll. I suggest just saying that anyone attempting to discern their nature suffers a penalty to the roll equal to their Simulacrum score. It covers messing with Mage Sight that way, or Auspex, or whatever Gifts Werewolves might bring, etcetera.<br /> <br /> Nobody senses supernatural nature through a Wits + Composure roll, that its used with Mortal Mask represents that there can/should be something wrong with an Ephemeral Being's imperfect mortal guise that even a mundane mortal can notice. Notably, mortals can't automatically tell if you're a Werewolf, a Mage or a Vampire through JUST a Wits + Composure roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a pullout box in <i>Blood and Smoke</i>. (Everything is in a pullout box. :\\ ) But yes --- that sounds like a sensible mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:51:45-08:00","id":358411,"title":"","content":"I should say I like the way the rest of it works. I think your idea for Buttressing is pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:54:07-08:00","id":358412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=358407#post358407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might be going too far with this particular part. Barring Vampires with other Vampires, we haven't actually seen anything that indicates supernaturals sense eachother's auras, merely that they can contest one another's auras with them. Vampires detect Vampires automatically because of theirs, but Mages require Mage Sight scrutiny and whatnot. Basically, you don't need to put this in terms of Wits + Composure, because sensing whether they're a supernatural being or not is <i>always </i>more involved than a simple Perception roll. I suggest just saying that anyone attempting to discern their nature suffers a penalty to the roll equal to their Simulacrum score. It covers messing with Mage Sight that way, or Auspex, or whatever Gifts Werewolves might bring, etcetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>I added the bit about Buttressing risk (i.e., exposure as a supe) because resisting would naturally show that there is something present. It provides a reason to sometimes sacrifice WP to keep oneself hidden.<br /> <br /> <b>Morphic Aura</b><br /> <br /> Purified exhibit an aura that many other supernatural beings can pick up on, but while in their physical bodies, their spirit nature attempts to conceal itself from other supernatural types. Attempts to discern their nature via supernatural means suffer a penalty to the roll equal to their Simulacrum while the Purified is embodied. In Twilight or Shadow, they are obviously supernatural.<br /> <br /> With Purified and embodied Spirits, the situation is different: Any Purified can sense a connection to Shadow and relative Chi/Rank with an unpenalized Intelligence + Occult roll, performed reflexively with skin-to-skin contact.<br /> <br /> Buttressing: Purified spirit natures will recoil in response to Lashing Out, the one-dot Discipline powers Awe and Dread Presence, and other powers that allow for a Predatory Aura-based resistance automatically. Not doing so requires the expenditure of 1 Willpower point. The resistance is based on Composure + Chi. If resisting Lashing Out, a Mage's Immediate Nimbus, &amp;c., Purified cannot impose Conditions, but they may receive the Conditions Showing or Threatened (as appropriate) if they fail their defensive roll. Buttressing automatically exposes them as another type of supernatural to whatever they are resisting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","user":"quantumelody","date":". 01-03-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:05:58-07:00","id":433345,"title":"","content":"WtF 2e was released this week! I have revised the mods I made for WoD2e for Purified based on its content, which provided a few more spirit-related things. Thanks, everyone, for the good conversation surrounding this.<br /> <br /> You can find the new revisions here: <a href=\"http://bit.ly/purified2e_hacks\" target=\"_blank\">http://bit.ly/purified2e_hacks</a><br /> <br /> And here is a short table of contents with some notes on what you might find of interest, as it occurred to me that not everyone will want to click on a PDF right off the bat. Also, this way, if people are searching for something on the forums, they might actually find the info in the PDF.<br /> <br /> <u><b>THE MODS</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Basic Hacks to the Immortals Text</b><br /> 1. Based on the GMC and WtF spirit information, along with others' mods of <i>Immortals</i> that seem to have worked out well (those posited here, for example), this provides a quick reference for innate Purified abilities.<br /> 2. The Morphic Aura that we discussed above<br /> <br /> <b>Spirits in Flesh</b><br /> 1. Essence: Harvest, addiction, and use<br /> 2. Banes, Bans, Restrictions<br /> 3. Influences<br /> 4. Chart of Chi for conversion to a 1-10 scale, &quot;Showing&quot; Influence-based spirit nature<br /> 5. Replacing Integrity with Simulacrum, which mashes up the Flesh:Spirit and slow degeneration from WtF and VtR respectively. (Purified are unique.)<br /> <br /> <b>Purified and Other Supernaturals</b><br /> 1. Some ideas on how their blood and other physical markers work<br /> 2. Changelings and Mages<br /> 3. What happens when Demons take a Purified as a Cover<br /> <br /> <b>General Purified Conditions</b> (I'm just listing these)<br /> 1. Essence Hunger<br /> 2. Influenced<br /> 3. Interested<br /> 4. Rapture Dependency<br /> 5. Spiritlike (Persistent)<br /> 6. Showing<br /> 7. Threatened<br /> <br /> <b>Hacks for Numina and Siddhi</b><br /> 1. General Numina guidelines to offer a reasonable expansion of the ones from core <i>Immortals</i><br /> 2. Additional Numina<br /> 3. Modifications for Siddhi to make them five-dot: They have been collapsed down to Siddhi of Flesh, Mind, and Will, and most of the 3-level Siddhi have been rolled into these. The ones that have not can easily be purchased as separate Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> 1. Awesome ones about possessions and professions<br /> 2. Curious merits that provide some supernatural benefits<br /> 3. Drink the kool-aid and learn kung fu from Scientologists! (AKA Purified Mystery Cults)<br /> <br /> <b>Thematics</b><br /> 1. Purification processes<br /> 2. Purified psychology: What's different, what's the same<br /> 3. SLANG. You know you want to read it!<br /> <br /> <b>The Human Artifice</b><br /> 1. An optional hack if people want to go further with Purified awesomeness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:48:55-07:00","id":433546,"title":"","content":"On-topic: with the release of Werewolf The Forsaken Second Edition, me and Aiden have started working on Harmony for Purified building on the original GMC hack. Also Dread Powers, as Gifts don't really work with them anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T03:48:48-07:00","id":433777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=433546#post433546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On-topic: with the release of Werewolf The Forsaken Second Edition, me and Aiden have started working on Harmony for Purified building on the original GMC hack. Also Dread Powers, as Gifts don't really work with them anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new version of Simulacrum above is (mostly) styled like new Harmony, but there is also a scale of penalties for human interaction and behavior. That part was cool about vampire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What kinds of Breaking points are you guys thinking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T06:43:11-07:00","id":433893,"title":"","content":"Don't have anything profound to contribute, just wanted to say that I came across this material a little while ago, and now our Purified player is excited about getting a bunch of new toys. Good job all around!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:23:04-07:00","id":433976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quantumelody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=433777#post433777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The new version of Simulacrum above is (mostly) styled like new Harmony, but there is also a scale of penalties for human interaction and behavior. That part was cool about vampire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What kinds of Breaking points are you guys thinking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most will provably adhere to the list of existing breaking points in WtF 2e Harmony or be very similar, but there's one or two that should only apply to werewolves so we'll be taking those out. We're thinking of placing the use of some powers as breaking points after certain levels of Harmony. The Projection Siddhi, vital as it is to the Purified condition, will also be affected by Harmony. High enough, you're going to have a hard time getting out of your body or even reforming it if you die. (Death and ressurecting are probably also going to be a breaking point.) With low Harmony, their spiritual weaknesses will become more severe or you'll gain more of them as Werewolves gain Bans.<br /> <br /> And eating human flesh for Essence (and only human flesh) will be an option, as well as a penalized breaking point the same way it is for Werewolves devouring human and wolf flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:43:10-07:00","id":434318,"title":"","content":"May I chime in to say that I don't think basing Simulacrum on Harmony is really all that thematic?<br /> <br /> It works for Werewolves because of their particular nature; it really is about <i>Harmony</i>. Whereas Simulacrum is probably closer to a Vampire's Humanity thematically; it's all about how good you are at <i>acting</i> human. If I'm off base, then Simulacrum is kinda... not a good name? It doesn't express the same concept as Harmony does, word-wise.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note... I like the formatting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:10:35-07:00","id":434377,"title":"","content":"I think my beef with is is that Werewolves are actually hybrids, so Harmony makes sense as keeping the balance between the two. Like Amechra says, if the emphasis is on the Purified not being human anymore, but basically humans transfigurated into spirits, then it's not a question of achieving harmony between your two halves, as you don't have two halves. You're one whole Spirit, clinging to the humanity it once had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-09-2015, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:25:03-07:00","id":434398,"title":"","content":"I like what I've seen so far of this, and if this ballooned into its own fangame, I'd pretty happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:20:35-07:00","id":434681,"title":"","content":"The reason Aiden and I decided to use Harmony as an alternative to Integrity with Octavo's GMC Purified Hack is because we believe there is thematically fitting conflict to be drawn from it. Purified aren't true spirits. But they aren't exactly humans anymore, neither in soul or body. This divide between their humanity and their closeness to spirits, and their need to balance it, live with the fact that they are forcibly part of both worlds, has always been a keystone of their existence far as we're concerned. How they chose to behave, and to what side of their dual life they are drawn towards is even more important for them than for Werewolves in some ways; because for the majority, becoming Purified to begin with was a deliberate, conscious decision. A change they might have dedicated themselves to and pursued for several decades.<br /> <br /> Their minds are affected by this change as well, forcing them to deal with things human perspective isn't equipped towards. Purified aren't natural. Being one has the logical consequence of causing your mentality to change to compensate; or to ground itself more strongly to retain your self-awareness as a human. Hence, Harmony. Because the balance between the different facets of what they are, or lack thereof, is important to a Purified's identity, and it makes sense that it would influence their state of being and their abilities reliant on thus.<br /> <br /> The premise we start from for the Purified is different from the one Kaye and Callishka assume in their much more extense mod. I also haven't really read it, so I don't know the details of Simulacrum; but what I remember of its narrative and thematic meaning doesn't really fit with Harmony, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-09-2015, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T17:11:20-07:00","id":434872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=434318#post434318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I chime in to say that I don't think basing Simulacrum on Harmony is really all that thematic?<br /> <br /> It works for Werewolves because of their particular nature; it really is about <i>Harmony</i>. Whereas Simulacrum is probably closer to a Vampire's Humanity thematically; it's all about how good you are at <i>acting</i> human. If I'm off base, then Simulacrum is kinda... not a good name? It doesn't express the same concept as Harmony does, word-wise.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note... I like the formatting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, the word Simulacrum's etymology is actually literal in this case. I think comparing it to Harmony in design is more effective because it captures that some things can cause mentally shattering moments in both directions (i.e., how do you really feel when you deny spirit influences?). That's why I kept the penalties for decreasing Simulacrum, Requiem-style. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T17:37:33-07:00","id":434887,"title":"","content":"NeoTiamat, malonkey1, I'm overjoyed that people are digging these Purified hacks. Somebody needs to run a Purified game using Octavo, YeOfLittleFaith /Aiden, or the quantum/callishka mods and report back to us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:05:54-07:00","id":434959,"title":"","content":"Our group had plans for a short Purified chronicle focused on tracking down and stopping a mysterious killer who had been dispatching immortals in the region, but it never really got off the ground. Right now we've been talking about a Werewolf chronicle and we have a pretty solidified concept to start with. Maybe Purified will be involved at some point and we can give feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:42:14-07:00","id":435009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=434681#post434681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise we start from for the Purified is different from the one Kaye and Callishka assume in their much more extense mod. I also haven't really read it, so I don't know the details of Simulacrum; but what I remember of its narrative and thematic meaning doesn't really fit with Harmony, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there are some moments of alignment in how we are approaching Purified, even if the core conceptual framework is different. It would be interesting to hear your thoughts after reading it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=434377#post434377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my beef with is is that Werewolves are actually hybrids, so Harmony makes sense as keeping the balance between the two. Like Amechra says, if the emphasis is on the Purified not being human anymore, but basically humans transfigurated into spirits, then it's not a question of achieving harmony between your two halves, as you don't have two halves. You're one whole Spirit, clinging to the humanity it once had.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on what I said to amechra above, one of the thought problems that I did not feel great about in the first version of this was actually some of the Simulacrum, and so I decided to leave it as-is until I had a good example of a push-and-pull system versus a degenerative one (although I would argue that mashing them up manages to do both). I had this core thought that Purified resisting the creation of Resonant Conditions, resisting Shadow, &amp;c., could cause a Breaking Point just as much as spiraling down into a humanoid spirit barely hanging onto the physical world, but it was difficult to scale at tier levels in a way that I found elegant.<br /> <br /> The Spirit Core of a Purified isn't a separate Beast; it's their own mind, and that's what is terrifying about it. There isn't an Other. There is only the terrifying realization that you cannot talk to someone in the checkout line at the grocery store because the fact that they are not buying pine-scented cleaner makes you feel a deep-rooted existential betrayal because their house will not smell like pine. You have three options: One, you can realize that the thought you just had is not human at all, leave the checkout line, and buy a floral-scented cleaner. Two, you can stay in the checkout lane and decide that humans just might not be that into your Influence (Pine), so you don't want their house to be Resonant with it, anyway. The hater. Third, you can indulge in that deeply inhuman reflex and let the existential betrayal turn into a tantrum of Numina or dirty looks. One side reinforces socially normal behavior and preserves/increases the Simulacrum, and one side does not, but neither leaves you feeling completely easy. (Having a conscience, even an artificial reflection of one, makes denying spirit impulses just as disturbing as overindulging ... until you slip one way or the other.) The middle path keeps things as they are.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think Purified care about processed food or associate it with being more human. That definitely had to go. I mean, for Outer Paths, Purification Juice is the least natural concoction a person can drink. ^____^ And I think the mods could be done either with a Humanity-style Simulacrum or a Harmony-style Simulacrum. The in-game situations will be just as complex and rewarding any way one slices it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:59:30-07:00","id":435967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=434887#post434887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NeoTiamat, malonkey1, I'm overjoyed that people are digging these Purified hacks. Somebody needs to run a Purified game using Octavo, YeOfLittleFaith /Aiden, or the quantum/callishka mods and report back to us!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've given them a bit of my own gloss, but I've a Purified player, so we'll see what happens. He's particularly excited about the fact that the Purified now have more in the way of actual supernatural 'heft', whereas before their main power vis-a-vis other supers was &quot;not dying.&quot; Which isn't irrelevant but isn't quite as exciting. The Essence/Influences/Simulacrum/Artifice Break (we're using that) material also excites me as the GM, because it reinforces the whole idea of &quot;Nope, you aren't human, sorry mate.&quot; And Influences go a long way towards making Purified distinct from one another in terms of behavior and aesthetic, which means there's room for more of them in the game.<br /> <br /> Now, admittedly, we've only got one Purified in the game, the PC, and they're supposedly rarer than hen's teeth. Still, I'm pondering situations where other Purified might pop up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:23:20-07:00","id":436496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=435967#post435967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, admittedly, we've only got one Purified in the game, the PC, and they're supposedly rarer than hen's teeth. Still, I'm pondering situations where other Purified might pop up.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Supposedly&quot;, being the operative word! Purified just have a really good Masquerade <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just have the Society of Spades invite your Purified PC to a meeting where they are all flipping out about rumors that thousands of Americans are building DYI assault rifles out of home-machined parts and 3D printed plastic. &quot;THE PLASTIC WAR IS UPON US WE MUST APPEASE THE ARTIFICIAL SPIRIT CHOIRS&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:59:11-07:00","id":436589,"title":"","content":"Something about that appeals to my sense of the ridiculous. I will have to try it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:20:59-07:00","id":437065,"title":"","content":"As I said when you shared the original gdoc, great work; I particularly appreciate your abilities to write engaging thematics and then back them up with solid mechanics. It takes a lot of balancing to do that.<br /> <br /> I did just notice that your Chi chart allows them to get up rank 10 spirits, and I'm curious as to what's behind that choice. Perhaps I've taken Dave B's comments on what level of power rank translates to too strictly as &quot;Word of God&quot;, but I'd feel that trying to reach higher than rank 6 is ground for a whole new game, &quot;Game of Immortals&quot; (changling) or Imperial Mysteries style.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a separate note, I've been using purified with a different philosophy as to their nature and influences and been having a hard time balancing it well. I've enjoyed exploring the &quot;spirits of humanity&quot; direction, but it ends up with way too many influences. If it's interesting to anyone, I'd appreciate help refining that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-11-2015, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:22:46-07:00","id":437176,"title":"","content":"I have to agree. No playable splat should outrank Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:44:22-07:00","id":437206,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, I've run into both issues in my game.<br /> <br /> &lt;&gt; I chopped Ranks roughly in half -- they track Werewolf Regen progression, actually, so my Chi 5 Purified is Rank 3, on the cusp of Rank 4.<br /> &lt;&gt; As for Influences, I had the Purified start as spirits of &quot;X&quot;, it being determined by their starting Influences. So my Purified is a Purified of Books (his pseudo-mentor) and Mercury (the poison that went into his ritual). I ruled that all further Influences or Numina had to branch out in some half-logical fashion from those, or else, like any Magath, he goes crazy. So his third Influence is of Exploration, and his Numina are mostly related to healing (mercury in Traditional Chinese Medicine) or knowledge-gathering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:26:10-07:00","id":437347,"title":"","content":"I take a very different approach with influence; my assumptions and goals regarding the Purified are rather different from Kaye and Callishka (and probably many of you). I'm exploring the 'spirits of humanity' angle, so I give Purified astral-like influences and those related to /who they are/ as people: narrative archetype, beliefs, virtue/vice, derangements, dreams, lifestyle, role. I took inspiration from the character aspects in Fate (DFRPG specifically; I'm not sure if that part differs any from Fate more broadly) and turned those into influences for the Purified. I'd phrase it as they have 'influences of identity' the way spirits' are of resonances and ghosts' are of anchors.<br /> <br /> It's worked with their presentation and role as I wanted to portray it, but as you can guess, it ends up allowing a large handful of various influences. The Purified in my game currently has 9 different influences. [I am fortunate that the player is a bit passive and doesn't fully comprehend the scope that gives her; I actually don't think she's used any of them in session, yet. She is more of a narrative, character growth and interaction driven player.] Now, I have to say part of that is because I'm playing a very high power level game (we're around 800 xp, 1E system). Still, this was allowed because of the broad philosophy I've taken with influences.<br /> <br /> So it's worked out thematically for what I want to present, but obviously allows <i>way</i> too much power. I've had a hard time trying to scale it back while still keeping the theme I'm aiming for.<br /> <br /> [For a more solid understanding of my approach, said Purified character has these influences: Fortitude, Envy (her Virtue and Vice), Shaman (social role), Trickster (narrative archetype and general activity), Snarker (personality), Tomboy (attitude and lifestyle), Wolf-Blooded (which should be rolled into Tomboy...), and Hobbesian (her world view / beliefs, especially about the shadow, and kind of a derangement/fear). The ninth is Technology - but she got that through a bargain with spirits at Best Buy; my hubristic little Purified is all grown up and becoming a magath~<br /> <br /> So, on the one hand, these Influences are kind of narrow, and they represent different aspects of a well fleshed-out character which (with the exception of Tomboy and Wolf-Blooded, and possibly Trickery and Snarker) would be hard to condense. People are complicated; you need a handful of aspects to summarize who they are, even in a shallow manner. On the other hand, that's a lot of influences, which are a very powerful and broad supernatural ability.<br /> It's a difficult balance to strike.]<br /> <br /> PS: I feel like noting that in the next chronicle I run which will include Purified, there will be very different base assumptions and goals for the template. I'm planning to use Kaye and Callishka's rules (with a few thematic tweaks) rather than what I've developed for that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-11-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:49:52-07:00","id":437707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=437065#post437065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did just notice that your Chi chart allows them to get up rank 10 spirits, and I'm curious as to what's behind that choice. Perhaps I've taken Dave B's comments on what level of power rank translates to too strictly as &quot;Word of God&quot;, but I'd feel that trying to reach higher than rank 6 is ground for a whole new game, &quot;Game of Immortals&quot; (changling) or Imperial Mysteries style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, agreed. It's way different at Chi 6+ in these mods. If people wanted to play very down-to-earth characters at a Chi that high, it would need to be modified.<br /> <br /> In addition, I think this is where the Mystery Cults can really shine. It would be interesting to have a game in which everyone is at MC 5, Chi 6+, and leads a cult of Purified to coordinate in response to threats and cult goals. In a game like that, the emphasis would include a lot of strategy (Suggestion: Do not start a land war in Asia!), and the power level would be so high that a lot of play would have to address issues like how to prevent power use that creates a shining beacon for Harvesters and other bad things. There are extremely high-level spirits that are now good antagonist candidates. At this level, Purified could also stand up really well in reality-bending God-Machine plot lines. So, it preserves a lot of the core of the World of Darkness, including the setting, while at the same time providing play aspects that are a bit reminiscent of the power level in Nobilis or Exalted with undertones of Fortune 500 CEO problems.<br /> <br /> It raises questions like: How do you teach and enrich your subordinates without growing frustrated that they're not at Int 8, Wits 7, and Resolve 6 like you? What is the balance between using Numina/Siddhi to control your Allies, Contacts, cult members, &amp;c. and relying on more genuinely human bonding strategies? What is stopping you from calling forth an entire block of sunlight at the next big vampire meeting because someone's ghoul gave you a parking ticket? You are (mostly) a spirit god, but does this leave you happy and fulfilled? How much of your time do you spend on things you enjoy, such as swimming with seals, versus managing the shit-storm that everyone throws on your lap?<br /> <br /> Not to mention that if you're a Purified at that level, the chances of you knowing how to effectively use modern technology are quite low, which is hilarious in a modern setting. If Purified at Simulacrum 0 lose access to their human bodies, maintaining Simulacrum at even 2 or 3 would be really, really hard for someone who falls into this category. How do you flirt with a girl in a coffee shop without using supernatural powers? How do you interpret that text message from your 15-year-old grandmentee? How are you going to wrap your mind around modern forms of finance management?<br /> <br /> And, of course, Purified like this are always good as NPCs: &quot;No, I want YOU to do that. No, I don't care if I could take care of it with a single phone call. This is about your personal development, and moreover, it cuts into my OWN skydiving time.&quot; ;D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=437065#post437065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a separate note, I've been using purified with a different philosophy as to their nature and influences and been having a hard time balancing it well. I've enjoyed exploring the &quot;spirits of humanity&quot; direction, but it ends up with way too many influences. If it's interesting to anyone, I'd appreciate help refining that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the mods I did, there is one basic way to expand into new Influences from the initial two: You gorge on an enormous amount of Essence. The eating could be either other spirits or a lot of Essence from a specific resonance. This requires a lot of RP justification. (Influences are also more powerful and easier to use if you stack dots in only the initial two, and so that's a plus.) The idea of insanity brought up later on by NeoTiamat is nice. Spirits just don't like eating stuff that they are not unless it means survival. EDIT: Ah, did not see that other page. Yes, agreed. Influences are very influential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","user":"quantumelody","date":". 03-11-2015, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:20:05-07:00","id":437736,"title":"","content":"Seraph Kitty--don't give up on your spirits of humanity angle. Before I got excited about quantummelody's brand of Purified and jumped on board to help flesh it out, my original idea was that Purified were the distilled essences of themselves as people--they were, essentially (no pun intended), more callishka than callishka, more Mary than Mary. I had the same idea that Purified were, deep down, spirits, but they were spirits of their former selves, which meant they had swapped the material/mind version for the pure spirit version. This intrigued me because it led me to think, if I were distilled to my truest, most characteristic traits, what would they be, and how would I feel if the older I got, the more I realized that I could never change--I could only become even more pure in those traits?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I find the idea of being walking nymphs of rivers, regret, steel, and other concepts more fascinating than walking expressions of personalities and dreams, but not by much. I say, run with your idea. If there are too many Influences, have the players pick two or three overriding ones to put their dots in. Those Influnces are the core of their personality, the hungriest part of them, the parts that burned through realities and became Pure and eternal. The other parts of them, not being eternal, are still crucial because those parts can evolve--those are perhaps even the more HUMAN traits they possess because they are NOT tied to an essence hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 03-11-2015, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T22:25:23-07:00","id":438050,"title":"","content":"I like that compromise a lot; it certainly holds to the intended concept, keeps a powerful stat limited, and gives a new motivation/conflict for characters to explore. I'd be hesitant to turn only a few personality aspects into influences and leave the others as sidelined, possibly fading details, but your presentation of it sells the idea well, with good highlights on the themes of trying to retain humanity while coming to terms with being an alien-minded hungering archetype. Thanks for the suggestion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T00:47:02-07:00","id":438167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=438050#post438050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be hesitant to turn only a few personality aspects into influences and leave the others as sidelined, possibly fading details</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the traits that don't become influences become... Virtue and Vice! The ritual renders eternal two or three traits (or one particularly mighty one), but there is always the human weaknesses and virtues, and these remain to give the character a personable dimension. For instance, if a Virtue: Fearless, Vice: Moody occultist happens to also be Funny and Tender, she could become a Purified who retains the same Virtue/Vice but whose Funniness and Tenderness become Influences, thereby making her a kind of minor god of warm-hearted laughter the older she gets. Her fearlessness is what impelled her to ritual suicide; her moodiness remains. On the other hand, she could acquire Influence (Fearless) 2, (Moody)1--making her a brave and stormy spirit-thing who happens to also have a sense of humor and a tender approach to some people. Or any combination thereof!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 03-12-2015, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:32:32-07:00","id":438374,"title":"","content":"Aye; I had originally turned Virtue and Vice into influences - that made <i>some</i> level of sense in 1E's classic 7 situation, but not necessarily a lot. They're important aspects of the personality, but then it belittles the concept of having them if the trait gets converted (or worse, replicated) to an influence. What I'm considering now is possibly allowing Virtue/Vice to give one point of Essence when they're evoked - no longer full influences, but a way for Purified to bolster their spiritual power through their own actions; a meager, but self-affirming advantage.<br /> <br /> After your suggestion, though, I'll totally borrow that imagery and be fine turning only a few traits into influences. Describing it as a person's &quot;hungriest&quot; most defining aspects becoming their spirit influences, while other important personality traits remain flexible, changeable, and ultimately more human evokes a great mood and allows for interesting internal drama.<br /> <br /> It lets the interesting situation of a person suddenly flipping their personality, because the things that used to be most important to them are now alien and frightening, so they try to highlight other aspects to reassure themselves of humanity. Or they become purified at an old age (or a really young one), which converts one of their cynical (/innocent) worldviews into an influence - it made complete sense for its context and age, but now that they're eternally in their mid 20s, those contexts have vanished, and they have eternally highlight an identity they no longer believe in, but need to express and draw out in others - something they learn as similar traits fade and change from new contexts and learning experience, but the influence remains: allowing a fun immortal who, despite being constantly betrayed, has to act like everyone is kind and noble; they 'learn', intellectually, that's not the case, and mentally prepare themselves to get cut down at the worst possible moment, but incapable of acting like it will.<br /> <br /> Ah, you have wonderful suggestions! I appreciate it the help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T08:03:50-07:00","id":438393,"title":"","content":"Unrelated,<br /> I've enjoyed chaining the Purified to spirit politics, and playing up how innate and deep that goes. I noticed that we both have the nascent purified discorporate and get flung to a random corner of the shadow, having to hike back to their body to fully complete the change. I had a lot of fun role-playing this experience for my player, introducing all kinds of threats, challenges, and moral conundrums to see what personality aspects she drew upon - and also to weave her into a tangle of obligations. I made it clear that without assistance, it was going to be a <i>rough</i> journey, and then I had several very different spirits 'offer' to help guide and protect her, in efforts to secure her service. She was, after all, a gaffling more likely to get eaten than ignored, but the higher-ranked spirits new how valuable an indebted purified could be.<br /> I present that as the normal prelude for most Purified, and assume that they come out of the ritual belonging to a choir, and literally owing their eternal life to one spirit or another. Not that they can't make it through on their own, but if someone returns without being massively indebted, that instantly earns a reputation.<br /> <br /> In fact, I was thinking about adding a secondary aspirations track, called &quot;Obligations&quot; for this very reason - and also to reflect the other bargains and business they've done since then, whether agreeing to help a ghost pass on, thanking a werewolf for letting them live, feeding rights at a locus they had to bargain for, or supernatural services they frequently sell. The unique experience (chimiage beats?) would be available to spend on merits and powers acquired in these deals, whether numina, resources, or leverage.<br /> With this track, you would't <i>need</i> to replace an Obligation once it's fulfilled - you can always choose not to make new deals - but you like the payment, right?<br /> <br /> Of course, the Obligations should scale with the original debt, but that could require some variability to when you can earn beats or how many they award. For example, my player accepted the help of a fading Toad incarnae (minor; rank 5), who taught her a few numen and fought off predators; in exchange for securing eternal life, it demanded she save the frog and toad species that were dying off from toxins in the environment. That could be represented by an Obligation which is forced to be replaced (the storyteller and player negotiate which deals that's necessary for), or the massive Obligation could just be worded as is and every step of significant progress awards a beat, or the completion of it gives 2 full experiences, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Although, particularly for the original life debt, these obligations can be acquired for benefits already received. So, I'd also recommend the optional rule of letting players go into exp debt; let them have a few free traits at the start - some extra numen, maybe the locus merit, as much as they want, at story-teller discretion - but the Obligation (and the accompanying leveraged condition) only goes away when all of it has been paid off using <i>only</i> chimiage experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, it could be an interesting additional track in general, regardless of template. It's not strictly necessary to put role-played negotiations into mechanical traits, but doing so could help speed along &quot;role-play earned&quot; traits [&quot;well, technically you've earned a dot of status with these guys, but do you have the exp for it?&quot;] - which I, and many other STs sometimes give out for free anyway, but still. And it would give players freedom and flexibility to start play in the middle of a bargain, and make more 'off screen' as they go.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-12-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:09:06-07:00","id":438756,"title":"","content":"Kaye's active Purified led my candidate through a ritual, and he ended up flung dozens of shadow miles away from his body. On his way back, he encountered the spirit of a frigid mountain lake that seemed unresponsive. He hiked on until he found himself looking at a barrage of spirit animals running toward him and away from an advancing wall of fire, ash, and lava spirits. It turned out the Yellow Stone volcano spirits and their attendant fiery friends were in eternal war with the spirits of the old ice sheet that covered Montana, and my char had stumbled into yet another reenactment of the turf war. He started running back the way he came, hitchhiked on the back of a deer-wind spirit who flung him way up, nearly back into the fire. He ended up back near the frigid lake, whose attention he couldn't get. Finally he threw a reflection of a stone into its mirror-still waters, and it woke up and allowed him into its surface on a raft of ice. The fire raged around them, then left. My char conversed with the old lake, finding that it would fall back into slumber after a period of inactivity, and it loved nothing more than to have its surface disturbed so that it could become still again. He agreed to come back every month to throw a rock in it, and after some negotiation it taught him End Disease, because this spirit also stills feverish tremblings.<br /> <br /> He then hiked back toward his body, but couldn't cross the Madison River until he answered three questions about water and rivers. He answered two (and learned Call Water and Pray for Rain) but then it asked him to tell it something about water it did not itself know. He couldn't find an answer and tried crossing to its opposite bank. It nearly destroyed him twice and sent him far away from where he wanted to be. Finally he just negotiated to cross in exchange for returning every month for ten years and giving chiminage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 03-12-2015, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:11:06-07:00","id":438760,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of obligations and debts. Kaye and I incorporate that into our playing without an explicit track for it, but it's a great way to get players to consider the price of being immortal AND linked eternally to a realm of greedy, demanding beings such as spirits. I'll reply more later!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:22:02-07:00","id":439021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=438393#post438393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the Obligations should scale with the original debt, but that could require some variability to when you can earn beats or how many they award. For example, my player accepted the help of a fading Toad incarnae (minor; rank 5), who taught her a few numen and fought off predators; in exchange for securing eternal life, it demanded she save the frog and toad species that were dying off from toxins in the environment. That could be represented by an Obligation which is forced to be replaced (the storyteller and player negotiate which deals that's necessary for), or the massive Obligation could just be worded as is and every step of significant progress awards a beat, or the completion of it gives 2 full experiences, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Although, particularly for the original life debt, these obligations can be acquired for benefits already received. So, I'd also recommend the optional rule of letting players go into exp debt; let them have a few free traits at the start - some extra numen, maybe the locus merit, as much as they want, at story-teller discretion - but the Obligation (and the accompanying leveraged condition) only goes away when all of it has been paid off using <i>only</i> chimiage experience.<br /> <br /> Actually, it could be an interesting additional track in general, regardless of template. It's not strictly necessary to put role-played negotiations into mechanical traits, but doing so could help speed along &quot;role-play earned&quot; traits [&quot;well, technically you've earned a dot of status with these guys, but do you have the exp for it?&quot;] - which I, and many other STs sometimes give out for free anyway, but still. And it would give players freedom and flexibility to start play in the middle of a bargain, and make more 'off screen' as they go.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea. I think that a Leveraged Condition makes sense for being severely indebted to specific spirits or choirs, but that on a daily basis, the ways in which those Conditions play out make sense using a list of goals to satisfy whatever one is beholden to. This is really nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:52:22-08:00","id":1041495,"title":"","content":"Bit of a thread necro here - I asked the talented Mr. Gone (Chris Leland) to create some character sheets suitable for Kaye and callishka's conversion of the Purified for CofD, and he has most graciously provided:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/NWoD_Immortals_Purified_2ndED_1-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/NWoD_Immortals_Purified_2ndED_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/NWoD_Immortals_Purified_2ndED_4-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12935-xardion","user":"Xardion","date":". 01-31-2017, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12935-xardion","name":"Xardion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T04:20:08-08:00","id":1041759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xardion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=1041495#post1041495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of a thread necro here - I asked the talented Mr. Gone (Chris Leland) to create some character sheets suitable for Kaye and callishka's conversion of the Purified for CofD, and he has most graciously provided:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/NWoD_Immortals_Purified_2ndED_1-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a><br /> <